# Backend API base URL for the frontend (Create React App).
#
# LOCAL DEVELOPMENT: leave empty. Relative /api/v1 requests are proxied to
# http://localhost:8000 by the CRA "proxy" field in package.json — no CORS.
#
# PRODUCTION (recommended — Vercel): leave EMPTY. The /api and /uploads
# rewrites in frontend/vercel.json forward same-origin requests to the Railway
# backend, so the browser only resolves the Vercel domain. Do NOT set this to
# a *.up.railway.app hostname: many ISP/enterprise resolvers fail on it and the
# browser shows net::ERR_NAME_NOT_RESOLVED.
#
# PRODUCTION (alternative — direct API): only set this if you use a custom API
# domain (e.g. https://api.yourdomain.com) that client networks can reliably
# resolve. Cross-origin CORS must then allow your Vercel origin.
REACT_APP_API_URL=
